    callout:{title:"Land restitution", body:"Since 1994, people removed after 1913 can claim land or compensation through the land restitution process — District Six claimants are still being resettled."},
    activity:"Interview an older family member or neighbour about where they lived before 1994 and whether they were ever forced to move. Write a short account.",
    activityAnswer:"Answers will vary. A good account includes place names, dates, reasons given for the move and how it affected the family's daily life.",
    examTip:"When using oral history or photographs as sources, comment on their usefulness and limitations (memory, perspective, purpose).",
    keyterms:[{w:"Forced removal",d:"Moving people from their homes by law and force"},{w:"Group Areas Act",d:"1950 law dividing towns into racial zones"},{w:"Land restitution",d:"Returning land or giving compensation to dispossessed people"}],
    quiz:[
      {q:"Sophiatown removals began in:",opts:["1948","1955","1976","1990"],a:1,et:"9 February 1955."},
      {q:"After the removals, Sophiatown was renamed:",opts:["Soweto","Triomf","Meadowlands","District Six"],a:1,et:"Meaning “triumph”."},
      {q:"District Six is in:",opts:["Johannesburg","Durban","Cape Town","Gqeberha"],a:2,et:"Declared white in 1966."},
    ],
